// The only automated check these four functions can have.
//
// supabase/functions/** is Deno, not Node: it imports from jsr:, uses the Deno
// global, and is excluded from tsconfig.json and from eslint.config.mjs on
// purpose — `tsc` cannot resolve `jsr:@supabase/functions-js` and would fail on
// every file. So the repo's own typecheck says nothing at all about ~1100 lines
// that verify payment slips, sync the rank database and wipe registrations, and
// a type error in them is first seen after the function is already deployed.
//
// `deno check` is the check that CAN run here. From the repo root:
//
//     deno task --config supabase/functions/deno.json check
//
// or, more simply, `cd supabase/functions && deno task check`.
//
// Deno is not installed on the maintainer's machine and there is no CI step for
// it yet; adding `denoland/setup-deno@v2` + this task to .github/workflows/ci.yml
// is what makes it actually run on every push. That file belongs to another
// part of the tree, so this is the half that lives here.
//
// Deploying is still manual (Supabase MCP deploy_edge_function or
// `supabase functions deploy <name>`), which is why the repo can drift from
// what is live — see docs/DEV-SETUP.md for the version each function is at.
{
  "tasks": {
    "check": "deno check admin-reset/index.ts purge-slips/index.ts sync-go-database/index.ts verify-slip/index.ts",
    "lint": "deno lint admin-reset purge-slips sync-go-database verify-slip"
  },
  "lint": {
    "rules": {
      "tags": ["recommended"]
    }
  }
}
